hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1425","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Muhammad bin Bishr told us, H, and Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i told us, Muhammad bin Bishr told us, Yazid bin Ziyad, who is Ibn Abi al-Ja`d, told us, on the authority of Zubaid al-Ayami, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ka`b ibn Ujrah, He said: Omar said, “The Eid al-Adha prayer is two rak’ahs, the Friday prayer is two rak’ahs, the Fitr prayer is two rak’ahs, and the traveler’s prayer is two complete rak’ahs, not shortening it.” The tongue of your Prophet, and he who slanders has been disappointed.”"
